1
00:00:01,220 --> 00:00:06,715
In 1997, the ocean made a sound no one could explain.

2
00:00:06,785 --> 00:00:11,361
Underwater microphones, built to hunt submarines, picked it up.

3
00:00:11,431 --> 00:00:16,736
It was so loud, sensors almost five thousand kilometres apart heard it.

4
00:00:16,806 --> 00:00:20,812
It came from one of the most remote places on Earth.

5
00:00:21,168 --> 00:00:23,061
Deep in the South Pacific.

6
00:00:23,131 --> 00:00:25,895
Its shape looked like an animal's call.

7
00:00:26,089 --> 00:00:27,318
They named it...

8
00:00:27,401 --> 00:00:28,404
the Bloop.

9
00:00:28,654 --> 00:00:31,843
But it was far louder than a blue whale.

10
00:00:31,926 --> 00:00:35,242
The loudest animal we know.

11
00:00:35,312 --> 00:00:37,925
So what is bigger than a blue whale?

12
00:00:37,995 --> 00:00:40,445
For years, nobody knew.

13
00:00:40,579 --> 00:00:44,256
And the internet decided it was a monster.

14
00:00:44,326 --> 00:00:48,839
Then, in 2005, scientists found the answer.

15
00:00:49,289 --> 00:00:50,610
It was ice.

16
00:00:50,884 --> 00:00:56,323
A giant iceberg, cracking and breaking apart, off Antarctica.

17
00:00:56,393 --> 00:00:59,100
The scariest sound in the ocean...

18
00:00:59,150 --> 00:01:01,325
was the planet, breaking.
